{"name":"Electric Light Orchestra","hex":"#f2e384","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"electric","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, produced by, operated with, or utilising electricity; electrical.","Of or relating to an electronic version of a musical instrument that has an acoustic equivalent."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electricity; the electricity supply.","An electric powered version of something that was originally or is more commonly not electric.\n An electric car, locomotive, train etc.\n\nAn electric toothbrush.\n\nAn electric typewriter."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/electric"},{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"orchestra","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large group of musicians who play together on various instruments, usually including some from strings, woodwind, brass and/or percussion; the instruments played by such a group.","A semicircular space in front of the stage used by the chorus in Ancient Greek and Hellenistic theatres."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orchestra"}],"entries":[{"title":"Electric Light Orchestra","blocks":[{"text":"Electric Light Orchestra (ELO) are an English rock band formed in Birmingham in 1970 by multi-instrumentalists Jeff Lynne and Roy Wood and drummer Bev Bevan. Their music is characterised by a fusion of pop and classical arrangements with futuristic iconography. After Wood's departure in 1972, Lynne became the band's sole leader, co-arranging and producing every album while writing nearly all of their original material. During their first run from 1970 to 1986, Lynne and Bevan were the group's only consistent members."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/ELO_1977.png/330px-ELO_1977.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electric_Light_Orchestra"},{"title":"Electric light","blocks":[{"text":"An electric light, lamp, or light bulb is an electrical device that produces light from electricity. It is the most common form of artificial lighting. Lamps usually have a base made of ceramic, metal, glass, or plastic that secures them in the socket of a light fixture. The electrical connection to the socket may be made with a screw-thread base, two metal pins, two metal caps or a bayonet mount."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Light-bulbs.jpg/330px-Light-bulbs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electric_light"},{"title":"Electricity","blocks":[{"text":"Electricity is the set of physical phenomena associated with the presence and motion of matter possessing an electric charge. Electricity is related to magnetism, both being part of the phenomenon of electromagnetism, as described by Maxwell's equations. Common phenomena are related to electricity, including lightning, static electricity, electric heating, electric discharges and many others."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/London_MMB_%C2%BB1E6_Lightning.jpg/330px-London_MMB_%C2%BB1E6_Lightning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electricity"},{"title":"Orchestra","blocks":[{"text":"An orchestra is a large instrumental ensemble typical of classical music or jazz, which combines instruments from different families. There are typically four main sections of instruments:"},{"items":["The string section, including the violin, viola, cello, and double bass","The woodwind section, including the flute, oboe, clarinet, and bassoon, and sometimes piccolo, cor anglais, bass clarinet, contrabassoon, and saxophone","The brass section, including the French horn, trumpet, trombone, and tuba, and sometimes cornet and euphonium","The percussion section, including the timpani, snare drum, bass drum, cymbals, triangle, tambourine, tam-tam and mallet percussion instruments"]}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/National_Chamber_Orchestra_of_Armenia.jpg/330px-National_Chamber_Orchestra_of_Armenia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orchestra"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Electric_Light_Orchestra_publicity_photo_1973.png/330px-Electric_Light_Orchestra_publicity_photo_1973.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Electric_Light_Orchestra_publicity_photo_1973.png/330px-Electric_Light_Orchestra_publicity_photo_1973.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Move/Electric Light Orchestra in 1972","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AElectric_Light_Orchestra_publicity_photo_1973.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Electric_Light_Orchestra_%281972%29.png/500px-Electric_Light_Orchestra_%281972%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Electric_Light_Orchestra_%281972%29.png/500px-Electric_Light_Orchestra_%281972%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"ELO in 1972. Top row left to right: Wilfred Gibson, Bill Hunt, Phil Copestake (roadie), Richard Tandy, Bev Bevan. Bottom row left to right: Hugh McDowell, Jeff Lynne, Roy Wood, Andy Craig","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AElectric_Light_Orchestra_(1972).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/ELO_in_1977_adj.png/500px-ELO_in_1977_adj.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/ELO_in_1977_adj.png/500px-ELO_in_1977_adj.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"August 1972 - May 1973 lineup of ELO. Top row left to right: Richard Tandy, Bev Bevan, Jeff Lynne, Mike de Albuquerque, Wilfred Gibson. Bottom row left to right: Colin Walker, Mike Edwards.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AELO_in_1977_adj.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Elo_27041978_04_800.jpg/500px-Elo_27041978_04_800.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Elo_27041978_04_800.jpg/500px-Elo_27041978_04_800.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"ELO performing in Oslo, Norway, in 1978","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AElo_27041978_04_800.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/ELO_-_Time_Tour_81-82.jpg/330px-ELO_-_Time_Tour_81-82.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/ELO_-_Time_Tour_81-82.jpg/330px-ELO_-_Time_Tour_81-82.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"ELO performing live during their 1981 Time Tour.From left: Jeff Lynne, Louis Clark (obscured), Kelly Groucutt, Bev Bevan, and Richard Tandy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AELO_-_Time_Tour_81-82.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Electric_Light_Orchestra_%281986%29.jpg/500px-Electric_Light_Orchestra_%281986%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Electric_Light_Orchestra_%281986%29.jpg/500px-Electric_Light_Orchestra_%281986%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"ELO performing in 1986 (Jeff Lynne and Richard Tandy pictured)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AElectric_Light_Orchestra_(1986).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Electric_Light_Orchestra_3.jpg/500px-Electric_Light_Orchestra_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Electric_Light_Orchestra_3.jpg/1280px-Electric_Light_Orchestra_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Electric_Light_Orchestra_3.jpg/500px-Electric_Light_Orchestra_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"ELO Part II in concert","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AElectric_Light_Orchestra_3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Electric_Light_Orchestra_in_2013_on_Stage.jpg/500px-Electric_Light_Orchestra_in_2013_on_Stage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Electric_Light_Orchestra_in_2013_on_Stage.jpg/1280px-Electric_Light_Orchestra_in_2013_on_Stage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Electric_Light_Orchestra_in_2013_on_Stage.jpg/500px-Electric_Light_Orchestra_in_2013_on_Stage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Orchestra during a performance in 2013","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w